h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.8 (build 612)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>One passphrase for everything.</b> A review now has a single spoken secret: four words, shown in the Shared Review panel while you host. The same words let someone join nearby, open a passphrase-protected link in a browser, or open it in Asobi. The six-digit passcode is gone. <b>Update both Macs</b> before joining nearby; a seat on an older build cannot connect to one on this build until it updates.</li>
<li><b>Passphrases forgive pasting.</b> A stray newline, tab, or double space in a pasted passphrase no longer counts as the wrong passphrase, in the app or in the browser.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
